Dogs already have a small avantage over cats: In the early game, when
you are most likely to be reliant upon your f or d for killing
monsters, you will encounter a lot more jackals, coyotes, foxes and
wolves than you will tigers, panthers and other f. Since pets won't eat
same-ascii corpses (unless desperate), this means dogs will leave you
more corpses to eat/ sacrifice than cats will. Of course this advantage
wears off in the mid game, where you can generally beat your pet to the
best corpses, but it's worth remembering that without a successful
early game, there _is_ no mid game.



